            "citations": null,
            "text": "# Two Key Aspects of Plate Tectonics\n\n1. **Lithospheric Plates in Motion**\n   - Earth's outer shell is divided into several large, rigid plates that float on the semi-fluid asthenosphere beneath them\n   - These plates move slowly (typically 2-10 cm per year) in various directions\n\n2. **Plate Boundaries and Geological Activity**\n   - Where plates interact (divergent, convergent, and transform boundaries), most geological activity occurs\n   - These interactions cause earthquakes, volcanic eruptions, mountain building, and ocean trench formation",
